---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Clearance.astro';
import Closer from '../../components/clearance/Closer.astro';
import { u } from '../../lib/url';
const c = (p = '') => u(`clearance/${p}`);
const lanes = [
  ['AGENT', 80], ['GITHUB APP', 220], ['GATE', 360], ['HUMAN', 500], ['ARGO · ADMISSION', 640], ['RECORDER', 780], ['LEDGER', 920],
] as const;
const msgs: [number, number, number, string, string?, boolean?][] = [
  [80, 220, 112, 'pull request opened'],
  [220, 360, 150, 'provenance + rendered tree'],
  [360, 220, 188, 'check: tier 2, with the reason'],
  [360, 500, 226, 'approval request'],
  [500, 360, 264, 'clears · IdP subject'],
  [360, 640, 302, 'grant: tree root · objects · env · policy · approver'],
  [360, 780, 334, 'decision recorded', 'muted'],
  [640, 780, 420, 'sync result via CDEvents'],
  [780, 920, 456, 'hash committed, witnessed', undefined, true],
];
---
<Layout title="How it works" page="how" description="How Clearance clears a change end to end: provenance, tiering on the rendered diff, the clearance token, three layers in Argo CD, gate providers, and what happens when something fails.">
  <style>
    .route-dot { offset-path: path('M80 120 H915'); animation: ride 7s cubic-bezier(.45,0,.55,1) infinite; }
    @keyframes ride { 0% { offset-distance: 0%; opacity: 0; } 5% { opacity: 1; } 55% { offset-distance: 60.5%; } 70% { offset-distance: 60.5%; } 95% { opacity: 1; } 100% { offset-distance: 100%; opacity: 0; } }
    .gate-pulse { animation: gp 7s ease-in-out infinite; transform-origin: 600px 120px; transform-box: view-box; }
    @keyframes gp { 0%, 52% { fill: var(--raised); } 58%, 68% { fill: var(--accent-soft); } 72%, 100% { fill: var(--clr-soft); } }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .route-dot, .gate-pulse { animation: none; } .route-dot { display: none; } }
  </style>

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="clr-wrap">
      <p class="kicker">How it works</p>
      <h1 class="display">Every change holds short until it's <em>cleared</em>.</h1>
      <p class="sub">The first release covers one route, end to end: GitHub to Argo CD to Kubernetes, for the environments you declare protected. Other paths, like a secret rotation or a Terraform apply, join through gate providers. Anything still outside is reported as coverage unavailable, in the record and in the packet, rather than quietly left out.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="clr-wrap" data-reveal>
    <figure class="fig">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 350" role="img" aria-label="A change taxis from pull request through provenance and classification to the gate. Policy clears tiers 0 and 1; tiers 2 and 3 wait for a named human. Admission checks every rendered object against its grant before the cluster applies it, and every step lands in the evidence record.">
        <defs>
          <marker id="hw-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="var(--rule-strong)"/></marker>
          <marker id="hw-r" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="var(--bad)"/></marker>
          <marker id="hw-g" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="var(--clr)"/></marker>
        </defs>
        <text x="20" y="36" font-size="17" fill="var(--ink)" font-weight="500">No change reaches the cluster without a clearance bound to it</text>
        <g fill="none" stroke="var(--rule-strong)" stroke-width="1.4" marker-end="url(#hw-a)">
          <path d="M140 120 H172"/><path d="M315 120 H347"/><path d="M490 120 H537"/>
          <path d="M600 182 V212"/>
        </g>
        <g fill="none" stroke="var(--clr)" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#hw-g)">
          <path d="M663 120 H702"/><path d="M835 120 H862"/><path d="M665 238 H768 V147"/>
        </g>
        <path d="M535 238 H80 V149" fill="none" stroke="var(--bad)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="5 4" marker-end="url(#hw-r)"/>
        <g fill="var(--raised)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)" stroke-width="1.3">
          <rect x="20" y="94" width="120" height="52" rx="10"/>
          <rect x="175" y="94" width="140" height="52" rx="10"/>
          <rect x="350" y="94" width="140" height="52" rx="10"/>
          <rect x="535" y="214" width="130" height="48" rx="10"/>
          <rect x="705" y="94" width="130" height="52" rx="10"/>
        </g>
        <polygon class="gate-pulse" points="600,58 663,120 600,182 537,120" fill="var(--raised)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="865" y="94" width="118" height="52" rx="10" fill="var(--clr-soft)" stroke="var(--clr)" stroke-width="2"/>
        <g font-size="13.5" fill="var(--ink)" text-anchor="middle">
          <text x="80" y="117">Pull request</text><text x="80" y="134" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--muted)">agent or person</text>
          <text x="245" y="117">Provenance</text><text x="245" y="134" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--muted)">with a confidence</text>
          <text x="420" y="117">Classify</text><text x="420" y="134" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--muted)">tier + policy verdict</text>
          <text x="600" y="116" font-weight="600">Hold short</text><text x="600" y="133" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--muted)">policy clears?</text>
          <text x="600" y="236">Named human</text><text x="600" y="252" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--muted)">not the initiator</text>
          <text x="770" y="117">Admission</text><text x="770" y="134" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--muted)">grant covers object?</text>
          <text x="924" y="117" font-weight="600">Applied</text><text x="924" y="134" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--muted)">protected cluster</text>
        </g>
        <g font-size="11.5">
          <text x="683" y="108" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--clr)" class="mono">T0–1</text>
          <text x="610" y="202" fill="var(--accent)" class="mono">T2–3</text>
          <text x="776" y="200" fill="var(--clr)">cleared</text>
          <text x="300" y="230" fill="var(--bad)">denied: back to the author, with the reason</text>
        </g>
        <circle class="route-dot" r="7" fill="var(--clr)" stroke="var(--raised)" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="20" y="284" width="963" height="52" rx="10" fill="color-mix(in srgb, var(--sky) 9%, transparent)" stroke="var(--sky)" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        <text x="38" y="306" font-size="11" class="mono" fill="var(--sky)">EVIDENCE RECORD · EVERY STEP</text>
        <text x="38" y="325" font-size="12.5" fill="var(--ink)">provenance · tier · policy version · approver · rendered tree · outcome · coverage and assurance state, witnessed</text>
        <g stroke="var(--sky)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 4" opacity="0.7">
          <path d="M245 146 V284"/><path d="M420 146 V284"/><path d="M770 146 V284"/><path d="M924 146 V284"/>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>Route · 01 of 04 · One change through the gate</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="clr-wrap">
      <div class="sec-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="kicker">The pieces</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Where each instrument <em>runs</em>.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cmp table-wrap" data-reveal>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Job</th><th>Runs</th><th>Leans on</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Provenance detector</td><td>Tags pull requests and commits; posts the check; registers as a GitHub deployment protection rule</td><td>GitHub App, hosted by default</td><td>Checks API, commit signatures, agent metadata, CI attestations</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Classifier and policy gate</td><td>Computes the tier; asks the policy engine; writes the decision and its reason</td><td>Your cluster</td><td>Kyverno or OPA, <code>clearance.yaml</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Binding plugin</td><td>Renders and hashes the tree, stamps the grant on every object, injects the wait, can fail generation on tier 3</td><td>argocd-repo-server sidecar</td><td>Argo CD Config Management Plugin</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Controller</td><td>Verifies each token and materializes a <code>ClearanceGrant</code>; a reconciler diffs live state for drift</td><td>Your cluster</td><td>Kubernetes, ValidatingAdmissionPolicy (CEL)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Gate providers</td><td>Bring other change paths under one record: native, federated or observed</td><td>Controller packages</td><td>Argo CD, Infisical, Spacelift, HCP Terraform, cloud audit logs</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Recorder</td><td>Append-only, signed record of every clearance event</td><td>Your cluster or hosted</td><td>Postgres (CloudNativePG), object storage</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Signer and ledger</td><td>Keyless signing; record hashes in a transparency log; checkpoints countersigned by consistency-proof witnesses</td><td>Clearance service</td><td>Sigstore, Tessera, C2SP witness formats</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Packet job</td><td>A date range to JSON, CSV and PDF, with control mappings and coverage</td><td>Recorder, batch</td><td>Mappings as versioned data</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Surfaces</td><td>Checks, chat approvals, the console</td><td>GitHub, Slack, Tower</td><td>Backstage plugin</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Identity</td><td>Approver identity through OIDC; subject and issuer recorded</td><td>Your IdP</td><td>Dex, Okta, Entra</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="clr-wrap">
      <div class="sec-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="kicker">The clearance token</p>
        <h2 class="h2">An approval tied to a PR number can be <em>outflown</em>. One tied to the rendered tree can't.</h2>
        <p class="sub">In GitOps, a new image tag and an edited ConfigMap are the same kind of event: a commit that renders to a different set of objects. So a clearance never binds to the image. It binds to the rendered desired state, at three levels, in a signed, short-lived token that also names the target, the policy version, the tier and the approvers. The recorder keeps the nonce so a token can't be replayed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="personas" data-reveal>
        <div class="persona"><span class="eyebrow">Level 1 · the commit</span><h3>What the approver saw.</h3><p>The git revision in the pull request, exactly as reviewed.</p></div>
        <div class="persona"><span class="eyebrow">Level 2 · the tree root</span><h3>The real subject.</h3><p>Every rendered object canonicalized and hashed, then the sorted hashes hashed into one root. A config-only change is a new root with the image unchanged inside it.</p></div>
        <div class="persona"><span class="eyebrow">Level 3 · each object</span><h3>What admission checks.</h3><p>Kind, namespace, name and rendered hash per object. The changed ConfigMap admits, the unchanged Deployment admits, anything not listed is refused.</p></div>
        <div class="persona"><span class="eyebrow">Cross-reference · the image</span><h3>A link, not the binding.</h3><p>Image digests ride along as extra subjects, so a supply-chain verifier can walk from build provenance to clearance.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sec-head mt-2" data-reveal>
        <p class="sub">Tiering reads the same tree. Clearance diffs it against the last cleared tree for that app and environment: a Secret or ClusterRole appearing is tier 3 however small the edit, replicas or a NetworkPolicy is tier 2, a log level is tier 1, and any change to an Argo Application is tier 3 because it changes the gated path.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="fig" data-reveal>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 590" role="img" aria-label="Sequence across seven lanes: agent, GitHub App, gate, human, Argo and admission, recorder, ledger. A tier 2 change is held, cleared by a human, bound to its rendered tree, admitted, applied and witnessed. In the alternate path a force-push renders a new tree, no grant covers it, and an exception is recorded.">
          <defs>
            <marker id="sq-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="var(--muted)"/></marker>
            <marker id="sq-r" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="var(--bad)"/></marker>
          </defs>
          {lanes.map(([name, x]) => (
            <g>
              <rect x={x - 60} y="40" width="120" height="30" rx="8" fill="var(--paper-2)" />
              <text x={x} y="59" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" class="mono" fill="var(--muted)">{name}</text>
              <line x1={x} y1="72" x2={x} y2="575" stroke="var(--rule-strong)" stroke-dasharray="3 5" />
            </g>
          ))}
          {msgs.map(([a, b, y, label, tone, below]) => (
            <g>
              <path d={`M${a + (b > a ? 4 : -4)} ${y} H${b + (b > a ? -6 : 6)}`} fill="none" stroke={tone ? 'var(--rule-strong)' : 'var(--muted)'} stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#sq-a)" />
              <text x={(a + b) / 2 + (below ? 12 : 0)} y={below ? y + 17 : y - 7} text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill={tone ? 'var(--muted)' : 'var(--ink)'}>{label}</text>
            </g>
          ))}
          <rect x="603" y="352" width="74" height="48" rx="7" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="640" y="372" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--ink)">render · bind</text>
          <text x="640" y="388" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--ink)">admit · apply</text>
          <rect x="743" y="436" width="74" height="26" rx="7" fill="var(--sky-soft)" stroke="var(--sky)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="780" y="453" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--ink)">sign record</text>
          <rect x="282" y="198" width="72" height="20" rx="6" fill="var(--raised)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)"/>
          <text x="318" y="212" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--ink)">tier 2 · hold</text>
          <line x1="20" y1="492" x2="980" y2="492" stroke="var(--bad)" stroke-dasharray="6 4"/>
          <text x="22" y="485" font-size="10.5" class="mono" fill="var(--bad)">ALTERNATE · TREE CHANGED AFTER APPROVAL</text>
          <path d="M84 520 H598" fill="none" stroke="var(--bad)" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#sq-r)"/>
          <text x="340" y="513" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="var(--ink)">force-push: a new tree renders at sync</text>
          <rect x="600" y="508" width="80" height="24" rx="6" fill="var(--raised)" stroke="var(--bad)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="640" y="524" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--bad)">no grant fits</text>
          <path d="M684 556 H774" fill="none" stroke="var(--bad)" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#sq-r)"/>
          <text x="730" y="549" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="var(--ink)">exception recorded</text>
          <text x="360" y="562" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="var(--muted)">held · re-evaluated as a new change</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>Sequence · 02 of 04 · A clearance is bound to the tree that lands</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="clr-wrap">
      <div class="sec-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="kicker">Inside Argo CD</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Three layers, each doing the <em>one</em> job it's good at.</h2>
        <p class="sub">A PreSync hook is the right place to show a wait and the wrong place to enforce one: it lives in the app's own manifests, <code>--strategy apply</code> skips it, and it can't see what it's gating. So a plugin binds at render, the hook shows the wait, and admission enforces at the API server, with no webhook on the hot path.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="fig" data-reveal>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 400" role="img" aria-label="Three layers in Argo CD. A commit is rendered by the Clearance Config Management Plugin, which binds the tree and stamps a grant on every object. A PreSync hook shows the wait for a human. A ValidatingAdmissionPolicy checks each object against a ClearanceGrant the controller materialized. A sync with strategy apply skips the hook but still meets admission. A kubectl apply by another identity is recorded as out-of-band.">
          <defs>
            <marker id="ly-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="var(--muted)"/></marker>
            <marker id="ly-g" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="var(--clr)"/></marker>
            <marker id="ly-r" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="var(--bad)"/></marker>
            <marker id="ly-m" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="var(--accent)"/></marker>
          </defs>
          <rect x="640" y="18" width="200" height="50" rx="10" fill="var(--raised)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)" stroke-width="1.3"/>
          <text x="740" y="39" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="var(--ink)">Clearance controller</text>
          <text x="740" y="56" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--muted)">verifies token · writes ClearanceGrant</text>
          <path d="M740 68 V104" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="4 3" marker-end="url(#ly-a)"/>
          <text x="748" y="90" font-size="10.5" class="mono" fill="var(--muted)">paramKind</text>
          <g fill="none" stroke="var(--clr)" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#ly-g)">
            <path d="M140 160 H176"/><path d="M392 160 H426"/><path d="M602 160 H636"/><path d="M842 160 H871"/>
          </g>
          <rect x="20" y="132" width="120" height="56" rx="10" fill="var(--raised)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)" stroke-width="1.3"/>
          <text x="80" y="156" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="var(--ink)">Git commit</text>
          <text x="80" y="173" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--muted)">the cleared PR</text>
          <rect x="180" y="106" width="212" height="108" rx="12" fill="var(--clr-soft)" stroke="var(--clr)" stroke-width="1.8"/>
          <rect x="430" y="106" width="172" height="108" rx="12" fill="var(--raised)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="6 4"/>
          <rect x="640" y="106" width="202" height="108" rx="12" fill="var(--clr-soft)" stroke="var(--clr)" stroke-width="1.8"/>
          <g font-size="10.5" class="mono">
            <text x="196" y="128" fill="var(--clr)">1 · BINDS</text>
            <text x="446" y="128" fill="var(--accent)">2 · SHOWS THE WAIT</text>
            <text x="656" y="128" fill="var(--clr)">3 · ENFORCES</text>
          </g>
          <g font-size="13.5" fill="var(--ink)">
            <text x="196" y="150">Config Management Plugin</text>
            <text x="446" y="150">PreSync hook</text>
            <text x="656" y="150">Admission policy</text>
          </g>
          <g font-size="11.5" fill="var(--muted)">
            <text x="196" y="170">in argocd-repo-server, at render</text><text x="196" y="187">hash the tree, stamp each object</text><text x="196" y="204">tier 3 can fail generation</text>
            <text x="446" y="170">a Job the plugin injects</text><text x="446" y="187">waits for a named human</text><text x="446" y="204">skippable, never the gate</text>
            <text x="656" y="170">ValidatingAdmissionPolicy, CEL</text><text x="656" y="187">a valid grant lists this object</text><text x="656" y="204">with this rendered hash</text>
          </g>
          <rect x="875" y="132" width="105" height="56" rx="10" fill="var(--raised)" stroke="var(--rule-strong)" stroke-width="1.3"/>
          <text x="927" y="156" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="var(--ink)">Protected</text>
          <text x="927" y="173" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--muted)">namespace</text>
          <path d="M286 214 V256 H720 V218" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="5 4" marker-end="url(#ly-m)"/>
          <text x="300" y="276" font-size="12" fill="var(--ink)"><tspan class="mono" font-size="11">argocd app sync --strategy apply</tspan> skips the hook, and still meets admission</text>
          <path d="M20 334 H927 V192" fill="none" stroke="var(--bad)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="5 4" marker-end="url(#ly-r)"/>
          <text x="30" y="326" font-size="12" fill="var(--ink)"><tspan class="mono" font-size="11">kubectl apply</tspan> by another identity: never reaches the plugin or the hook</text>
          <text x="30" y="358" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--muted)">Not denied by default, because that breaks every emergency. The reconciler records it as out-of-band, or as break-glass when</text>
          <text x="30" y="375" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--muted)">someone took that path. Want it refused outright? Flip one field.</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>Layers · 03 of 04 · Argo CD integration, and where each layer can be bypassed</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="cols mt-2" data-reveal>
        <div><p class="kicker">Neighbours, not rivals</p></div>
        <div>
          <p>Teams running Kargo get Clearance as a promotion step and a verification, with the same token and the same recorder. Argo CD Notifications feeds sync results to the recorder for teams that don't emit CDEvents. Later, an Argo UI extension shows the tier, the approver and a clear button on the application page, approving as the signed-in Argo user. <span class="chip proposal">Proposal</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="clr-wrap">
      <div class="sec-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="kicker">Gate providers</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Not every change is a commit. Every change gets the <em>same</em> record.</h2>
        <p class="sub">A secret rotates in Infisical. A Terraform plan applies through Spacelift. Each path already has its own approvals, and the humans already trust them there. Clearance doesn't rebuild those. Every path fills one five-part contract, so the tiers, the record and the packet stay the same whatever the route. A provider that can't fill a part says so, in the coverage statement.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bento" data-reveal>
        <div class="tile span-2"><p class="kicker">Native</p><h3>Clearance is the enforcer.</h3><p>It binds, enforces and writes full records. Argo CD first; Flux and Kargo next.</p></div>
        <div class="tile span-2"><p class="kicker">Federated</p><h3>Your system approves, Clearance proves it.</h3><p>It checks the posture, ingests approvals and applies, matches them to what landed, and attests it was authorized under that system's policy. Infisical, Spacelift, HCP Terraform, GitHub environments, Vault.</p></div>
        <div class="tile span-2"><p class="kicker">Observed</p><h3>Seen, and said so plainly.</h3><p>No authorization claim, only coverage: which change, by which identity. Cloud audit logs, and anything else you want in the packet.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cmp table-wrap mt-2" data-reveal>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Contract</th><th>Argo CD · native</th><th>Infisical · federated</th><th>Terraform · federated</th><th>Cloud audit log · observed</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Proposal</td><td>Pull request, rendered tree</td><td>Change request on a protected path</td><td>Plan on a run</td><td>None</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Bound subject</td><td>Commit, tree root, per-object hashes</td><td>Request id and secret version, never the value or its hash</td><td>Plan digest and state serial</td><td>Resource id and event id</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Enforcement</td><td>Clearance: plugin and admission</td><td>Infisical's own approval policy</td><td>The platform's approval policy</td><td>None</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Evidence</td><td>Argo Notifications, CDEvents</td><td>Audit webhooks, change-request API</td><td>Run events, audit trail</td><td>The cloud's audit log</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Coverage</td><td>Opted-in apps in protected environments</td><td>Paths under hard-enforcement policies</td><td>Stacks with approval policies</td><td>What the log saw; no authorization claim</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="cols mt-2" data-reveal>
        <div><p class="kicker">Worked through: Infisical</p></div>
        <div>
          <p>A rotation never touches git, which is right, and it's why Argo alone would report it as out-of-band. With the Infisical provider, the agent's call passes the Clearance runtime gateway on its way in, which stamps a task id into the change request. Four events in three systems then line up without guessing, and the rotation is attributed instead of flagged.</p>
          <p>Posture is a finding, not a second approval screen: a secret path a protected environment depends on that isn't under a hard-enforcement policy shows up in the packet as a coverage gap. Infisical comes second, after Argo CD; the rest arrive when a design partner needs them. <span class="chip proposal">Proposal</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
